  "raw_answer": "C1|Coarctation of the aorta is a congenital narrowing of the aortic lumen caused by thickening of the tunica media near the junction of the ductus arteriosus and the aortic arch, leading to mechanical obstruction of blood flow.|Passage 1|\nC2|It is associated with a patent ductus arteriosus, located distal to the aortic arch and proximal to the PDA, and has a frequent association with Turner syndrome.|Passage 1|\nC3|In infants, lower extremity exercise intolerance may suggest coarctation of the aorta, but the context only partially covers diagnostic evaluation.|Passage 1|",
